    "input": "search_document: I understand your frustration regarding the suspension of your account and the inability to access your order details. Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the information regarding your situation:\n\n**Account Suspension and Reactivation**\nAccording to the **Accounts** section, if an email is not verified within 24 hours of registration, the account is automatically suspended [accounts.1]. However, the handbook states that you may reactivate the account by resending the verification link [accounts.1]. It is important to note that if the account remains unverified for 7 days, it is permanently deleted, and any associated draft orders are canceled [accounts.1]. Since you mentioned you just purchased the items, I assume the 7-day window has not yet passed, meaning your account is likely still recoverable via the verification link rather than being permanently deleted.\n\n**Access to Order Details**\nThe handbook does not provide a specific procedure for accessing order details while an account is suspended, other than the reactivation method mentioned above. It does not state that providing ID or proof of purchase is a standard requirement for reactivating a suspended account due to unverified email; that process is specifically outlined for losing access to a 2FA device [accounts.3].\n\n**Request for Human Callback**\nThe handbook excerpts provided do not contain any policies, contact information, or service level agreements regarding human agent callbacks, phone support, or response times for customer service requests. Therefore, I cannot confirm or arrange a human callback within the hour based on the available documentation.\n\n**Next Steps**\nTo resolve the suspension, you should attempt to resend the email verification link as described in the **Accounts** section [accounts.1]. If this does not resolve the issue, or if you require further assistance that is not covered by the standard reactivation process, I must inform you that the provided handbook excerpts do not cover escalation procedures or human support contact methods. I recommend escalating this ticket to a human agent who can review your specific account status and order history, as the current documentation does not provide a mechanism for me to override the suspension or arrange a phone call.",
